+When the user authorizes execution, keep improve advisory/read-only and dispatch writing work through Orca. The lead Pi session must bind an explicit Orca Run, create bounded Tasks from the reviewed plan, and start workers in Orca-managed isolated worktrees using the configured Pi launcher/model; do not hard-code a host-specific `general-purpose` agent or `sonnet` model name.
+
+Each Orca worker brief should include the selected plan slice, exact repo/base ref, owned files, prohibited files/data, verification commands, report requirements, and STOP/ask conditions. Workers use Orca's injected `ask` and `worker_done` contract and do not load the improve skill as their execution role.
+
+The lead reviews worker reports and diffs, asks decision gates when needed, dispatches revisions or an integration worker when explicitly authorized, and leaves merge/push/publication authority with the human.
